//
// QWEN3-4B Q4NX prefill TTFT vs padded prefill length, into
// qwen3_4b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
//
// The other axis from run_npu2_sweep.lit: that one walks KV depth for decode
// tok/s, this one walks the length the prefill ELFs are BUILT for. They cannot
// share a table -- one is throughput against cache depth, the other is latency
// against problem size.
//
// This model already had the decode sweep and a working `profile-prefill`
// target; only the lit was missing. Without it the model kept a single-point
// row in the scalar table, and that point is the profile prompt -- 24 tokens.
// A TTFT measured at 24 tokens sitting in the same section as curves measured
// at 512-4096 invites reading them as comparable, which they are not. With this
// file the scalar table has no rows left at all.
//
// Unlike the bf16 models' prefill sweep, this path has no median/min: the q4nx
// prefill driver times itself rather than going through
// shared/infra/prefill_bench.py. Still worth unifying, but note the open item
// it was first cited for turned out NOT to be a measurement problem:
// lfm2_1_2b_q4nx publishes 81871 ms at 4096 against 1112 ms at 2048, and that
// REPRODUCES -- 81794 ms on an idle second machine. The 2048 point differs 18%
// between the two boxes and the 4096 point differs 0.1%, which is the signature
// of a deterministic fixed cost, not contention. It is a real cliff and wants
// its own investigation.
//
// Latency only, never a correctness gate (run_npu2_verify.lit is that). The
// per-length first-token argmax the driver already prints is recorded with each
// point; all four passed when this file was written.
//
// Measured on a Ryzen AI 9 HX 370: 1711 / 2861 / 5886 / 13077 ms at
// 512 / 1024 / 2048 / 4096.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, llvm_link_pre23, hf_token, hfweights_fastflowlm_qwen3_4b_npu2
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name qwen3_4b_q4nx --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048,4096 --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out qwen3_4b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < qwen3_4b_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "qwen3_4b_q4nx"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number at the reference length, not just a well-formed file: if the
// driver's TTFT line drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes
// null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
